cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TerraFlow in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TerraFlow: A Reproducible Workflow for Geospatial Agricultural Modeling"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-02-24"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gmarupilla/AgroTerraFlow"
url: "https://terraflow.marupilla.dev"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.18490119
abstract: >
  TerraFlow is an open-source Python library for reproducible, auditable geospatial
  workflows in agricultural and environmental data science. It provides a
  config-driven pipeline for raster ingestion, ROI clipping, spatial climate
  interpolation, suitability scoring, and provenance-tracked artifact export.
  Every run produces a deterministic content-addressed fingerprint enabling
  independent verification of results.
keywords:
  - geospatial
  - agriculture
  - reproducibility
  - raster
  - climate
  - workflow
  - Python
authors:
